From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:34:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: exynos5: Add Exynos9820 support

The buses of this SoC take the timing path of the newer variant, which
programs the divider and leaves the two registers holding the SCL periods
alone.

Which one it is was measured rather than chosen by family, because writing
the lower period register is not merely wrong here, it wedges the block:
with any value other than the one reset leaves in it, the controller stops
driving the pins altogether, keeps the master-busy flag set forever and
never empties the transmit FIFO.  Every address then looks like a bus with
nothing on it.  Writing that same register back with the value it already
holds is harmless, and so is programming the other three, so it is that one
register and not the amount of programming that the hardware objects to.

With the divider alone, a scan of the bus the main PMIC sits on answers
from four devices, at the addresses the board describes and at the same
ones a transfer generated by hand on those pins answers from.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
index 9c1c5f3c09f..20f8d4af6c2 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-exynos5.c
@@ -265,6 +265,20 @@ static const struct of_device_id exynos5_i2c_match[] = {
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "samsung,exynos8895-hsi2c",
 		.data = &exynos8895_hsi2c_data
+	}, {
+		/*
+		 * Measured on the phone, not chosen by family.  This SoC
+		 * wants the variant that programs the divider and leaves
+		 * the two SCL period registers alone: writing the lower one
+		 * at all, with any value other than the one reset leaves
+		 * there, wedges the controller.  It then stops driving the
+		 * pins entirely, keeps the master-busy flag set forever and
+		 * never empties the transmit FIFO, which looks exactly like
+		 * a bus with nothing on it.  With the divider alone the same
+		 * scan answers from four devices.
+		 */
+		.compatible = "samsung,exynos9820-hsi2c",
+		.data = &exynosautov9_hsi2c_data
 	}, {},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, exynos5_i2c_match);
